{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-112947-r4514984","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Olive Ascolane (Stuffed Fried Olives)","sourcePageId":112947,"sourceRevision":"4514984","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T02:54:22Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Olive%20Ascolane%20(Stuffed%20Fried%20Olives)&oldid=4514984","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:41.963Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Appetizer recipes","Category:Italian recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Pan fried recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using allspice","Category:Recipes using bread crumb","Category:Recipes using canola oil","Category:Recipes using chicken breast","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using lemon zest","Category:Recipes using olive","Category:Recipes using parmesan","Category:Recipes using pork","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"ffec4a0e78673e7f8bc37cccda8a47f584ab40e8e2d07bc35503791105d0a5f2","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Yield = 50 stuffed olives\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Olive ascolane''' is an Italian starter from Ascoli Piceno made of fried green olives, stuffed with minced meat (beef, pork and chicken liver) and spices. This recipe was contributed to [http://www.italiansrus.com ItaliansRUs.com] by Phil and Jackie Cicconi.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Filling ===\n* [[Cookbook:Sauces#Tomato-based sauces|Tomato sauce or gravy]]\n* 1 ½ [[Cookbook:Pound|pounds]] [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]]\n* 1 ½ pounds [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken breast]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] green olives\n* ⅔ cup Parmesan [[Cookbook:cheese|cheese]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]] rind, [[Cookbook:Grating|grated]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] freshly-grated [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Allspice|allspice]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n\n=== Base ===\n* About 50 large pitted green [[Cookbook:Olive|olives]], halved{{efn|Have an extra jar of olives on hand in case you are left with extra filling.}}\n\n=== Breading and frying ===\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Eggs|eggs]], beaten\n* [[Cookbook:Flour|Flour]]\n* Plain [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|bread crumbs]]\n* [[Cookbook:Rapeseed Oil|Canola oil]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n#Cook the pork and chicken breast in your favorite tomato gravy recipe.\n# Remove cooked, cooled meats from the sauce and grind them using a meat grinder or [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]].\n# Add the remaining filling ingredients to the ground meat mix (do not over-process). Mix the ingredients into the meat and put into the refrigerator to cool for at least one hour.\n# Remove the mixture from refrigerator and roll meat into balls about the size of a small walnut. Put half of an olive on each side of the rolled ball.\n# Flour each ball, dip in beaten egg, then dip in bread crumbs. \n# Arrange olive balls on a tray.{{efn|Stuffed olives can be frozen unfried at this time. Allow frozen olive balls to completely defrost before frying.}} [[Cookbook:Pan Frying|Fry]] them quickly in about ½ inch of canola oil until golden brown.{{efn|It is not important to cook them through because the meat has been cooked already.}}\n# Drain and serve.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n[[Category:Italian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using olive]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken breast]]\n[[Category:Appetizer recipes]]\n[[Category:Pan fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using allspice]]\n<references group=\"note\" />\n[[Category:Recipes using parmesan]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using canola oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon zest]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Olive Ascolane (Stuffed Fried Olives)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Tomato sauce or gravy","sourceText":"Tomato sauce or gravy","amountText":"Tomato sauce or gravy","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 ½ pounds pork","sourceText":"1 ½ pounds pork","amountText":"1 ½ pounds pork","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 ½ pounds chicken breast","sourceText":"1 ½ pounds chicken breast","amountText":"1 ½ pounds chicken breast","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ cup chopped green olives","sourceText":"½ cup chopped green olives","amountText":"½ cup chopped green olives","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"⅔ cup Parmesan cheese","sourceText":"⅔ cup Parmesan cheese","amountText":"⅔ cup Parmesan cheese","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 lemon rind, grated","sourceText":"1 lemon rind, grated","amountText":"1 lemon rind, grated","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 teaspoon freshly-grated